# Netlify redirects.
#
# THIS FILE CANNOT CATCH THE URLS THAT MATTER, AND THAT IS NOT A CONFIGURATION
# MISTAKE. The site uses hash routes (#/category/:id). A URL fragment is never
# transmitted to the server, so Netlify cannot see or match it — a rule for
# /#/category/resilience is unreachable by construction, and writing one would
# be a check that looks like it works and never fires (rule 20).
#
# The retired-slug redirects that actually fire are CLIENT-SIDE, in
# js/views/category.js, driven by data/retired-categories.json.
#
# The rules below cover the PATH form only — what an external tool, a crawler
# or a hand-typed link may produce. Those are real requests, they do reach the
# server, and they are cheap to handle.

/category/remote-work   /#/category/deep-work-and-focus    301
/category/resilience    /#/category/emotional-regulation   301
/category/delegation    /#/category/people-management      301
